    Kuna #850: the branch at 0x10008 targets a separately discovered entry inside the
    asserted outer function.  It is an ordinary local edge, so tailcalljump
    must keep both return paths.  A second, exact four-byte veneer branches to
    a known helper outside its declared extent; that transfer remains a tail
    call when the option is on.

      0x10000 outer:       cmp r0,#0; bne 0x1000c; b 0x10014
      0x1000c               mov r0,#3; bx lr
      0x10014 interior:    mov r0,#7; bx lr
      0x10020 veneer:      b helper
      0x10028 helper:      mov r0,#9; bx lr

    Stage: P2 flow classification. P0 assertion: `option tailcalljump on|off`.
    The enabled outer pass reproduces the pre-fix misclassification; the off
    pass is the control. Assertion #1 fails before the fix; #2 keeps the other case. Assertion #3
    ensures that the out-of-extent veneer remains recognized as a tail transfer.
    The read-only literal jump at 0x10200 targets a stated interior entry at
    0x10210 inside the outer extent. Assertions #4/#5 require that recovered
    indirect destination to remain local as well.
-->
